---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import StepsStrip from '../components/StepsStrip.astro';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Why would I start at a number other than 1?',
    a: 'When this file continues another one: an appendix that follows a 40-page report starts at 41, so the pack reads straight through. The first page stamped gets the number you type; the rest follow on.',
  },
  {
    q: 'In "Page X of Y", what is Y?',
    a: 'The last number stamped, counting only the pages you numbered. Number a whole 12-page file from 1 and the pages read "Page 1 of 12" to "Page 12 of 12". Number only pages 5 to 12 of it, starting at 5, and they read "Page 5 of 12" to "Page 12 of 12".',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can the numbers be taken off later?',
    a: 'Not by a switch: they are drawn onto the pages, the same way flattening bakes in a form\'s answers. Editing them off means editing the pages themselves. Keep your unnumbered original, and number a copy.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where does my document go?',
    a: 'Nowhere. It is read into this page and numbered in your browser. Watch the network panel while it works if you want to check.',
  },
];
const faqJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faq.map((f) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: f.q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a } })),
});
const howToJson = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'HowTo',
  name: "How to add page numbers to a PDF",
  step: [
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 1, name: "Pick the PDF", text: "Drop a PDF on the tray, or click to pick one. It stays on this device. The page reads its page count before anything runs." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 2, name: "Choose the numbers", text: "Pick where they sit (bottom centre, bottom outside corner, or top centre), how they read ('Page X of Y', 'X of Y', or a plain number), the number to start from, and whether every page or one range is numbered." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 3, name: "Add the numbers", text: "Press 'Add the page numbers'. Each number is drawn onto its page as ordinary content and the file is saved." },
    { '@type': 'HowToStep', position: 4, name: "Download the numbered PDF", text: "Take the finished file away, and keep your unnumbered original: drawn-in numbers are part of the pages now." },
  ],
});
---

<Base title="Add page numbers to a PDF, free · Benchzy" description="Stamp page numbers onto a PDF, bottom centre, outside corners or top, as 'Page X of Y' or a plain number, starting where you say, inside your browser. The numbers are drawn onto the pages themselves.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4">
    <section class="mt-8">
      <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-accent-deep">PDF tools · pages</p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-black mt-2">Add page numbers</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        Put page numbers on a finished PDF: pick where they sit, how they read, and the
        number to start from. The numbers are drawn onto the pages themselves, in your
        browser; the document is never uploaded.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="ticket mt-6 p-5 sm:p-7" id="pn-tool">
      <div id="pn-tray" class="tray p-6 text-center cursor-pointer" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Pick a PDF">
        <p class="font-display text-xl font-bold">Drop a PDF on the tray, or click to pick one</p>
        <p class="font-mono text-xs text-ink-soft mt-2">PDF · it stays on this device</p>
        <input id="pn-file" type="file" accept="application/pdf,.pdf" class="hidden" />
      </div>
      <p class="file-loaded hidden" data-loaded-for="pn-file" role="status"></p>

      <div class="grid gap-6 mt-6 md:grid-cols-[1fr_320px]">
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">Where they sit</h2>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="pn-pos" value="bottom-centre" checked />
              <span>Bottom centre</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="pn-pos" value="corners" />
              <span>Bottom outside corner (right on odd numbers, left on even, the way books print it)</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="pn-pos" value="top-centre" />
              <span>Top centre</span>
            </label>
          </div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft mt-6">How they read</h2>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="pn-format" value="page-of" checked />
              <span>Page X of Y</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="pn-format" value="of" />
              <span>X of Y</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="pn-format" value="plain" />
              <span>A plain number, X</span>
            </label>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 ml-6 flex-wrap">
              <label class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft" for="pn-start">Start at</label>
              <input id="pn-start" type="number" min="0" step="1" value="1" class="border border-ink bg-ticket px-3 py-2 font-mono w-24" />
            </div>
          </div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft mt-6">Which pages</h2>
          <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3">
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="pn-scope" value="all" checked />
              <span>Every page</span>
            </label>
            <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
              <input type="radio" name="pn-scope" value="range" />
              <span>One page range</span>
            </label>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 ml-6 flex-wrap">
              <label class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft" for="pn-from">From page</label>
              <input id="pn-from" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="1" class="border border-ink bg-ticket px-3 py-2 font-mono w-24" />
              <label class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft" for="pn-to">To page</label>
              <input id="pn-to" type="number" min="1" step="1" value="1" class="border border-ink bg-ticket px-3 py-2 font-mono w-24" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h2 class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-ink-soft">File spec</h2>
          <dl id="pn-spec" class="mt-2">
            <div class="spec-row"><dt>file</dt><dd>none picked yet</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="action-note">
            The numbers become part of the pages, like ink: they cannot be switched off
            afterwards. Keep your unnumbered original, and number a copy.
          </p>
          <button id="pn-run" class="btn-primary w-full mt-5" type="button" disabled>Add the page numbers</button>
          <p id="pn-status" class="font-mono text-sm mt-4 leading-relaxed" aria-live="polite">Pick a PDF to begin.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div id="pn-result" class="receipt hidden mt-8">
        <div class="tear pt-5 flex items-center gap-4 flex-wrap">
          <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold">Result</h2>
          <span class="stamp" id="pn-stamp">Done on your device</span>
        </div>
        <p id="pn-achieved" class="mt-3 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl"></p>
        <a id="pn-download" class="btn-primary inline-block no-underline mt-3" href="#" download>Download the numbered PDF</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <StepsStrip who="For a report, a contract pack or a court bundle that people must refer to by page ('see page 14'), which came off the printer with no numbers on it." steps={[{ n: '01', t: 'Pick the PDF' }, { n: '02', t: 'Choose the numbers' }, { n: '03', t: 'Number and download' }]} />

    <section class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">How it works</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          The page writes each number straight onto its page as ordinary page content, at
          the place you picked, then saves the file. The download is how we protect your
          privacy: the program that does this job is part of this page, loaded from this
          site, and your file is read into the page and never uploaded. Because the numbers
          are drawn in, they print with the file everywhere and cannot fall off; they are
          not form fields, and they do not change when the file is copied.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Honest limits</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
          Drawn-in numbers are part of the page now: taking them off later means editing
          the pages, so keep your unnumbered original. The numbers count the file's pages
          as they stand when you run this; if you merge or cut pages afterwards, run it
          again on the finished file so the numbers still match the pages.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">A password-protected PDF cannot be opened by this tool. Take its password off first with the <a class="underline underline-offset-4" href="/unlock-pdf/">unlock tool</a>, then bring the file back.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-10 mb-4">
      <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-bold border-b-2 border-ink pb-2">Questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-4 grid gap-4">
        {faq.map((f) => (
          <article class="ticket-soft p-5">
            <h3 class="font-bold">{f.q}</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-soft leading-relaxed mt-1">{f.a}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqJson}></script>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={howToJson}></script>
  <script>
    import '../scripts/pdf-page-numbers.js';
  </script>
</Base>
